  "description": "CHANGE OF USE OF ANCILLARY GARDENROOM TO CREATE A NEW TWO BEDDWELLING",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Wimbledon Park",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:29:15.849Z",
  "street_name": "DURNSFORD ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The proposed development, by reason of its location within the rear garden; its separation from the established residential frontage; and its reliance on a narrow pedestrian access, would result in an inappropriate form of development which fails to respect the prevailing pattern, layout and character of development in the surrounding area. The introduction of an independent dwelling in this location would undermine the established relationship between principal residential buildings fronting Durnsford Road and the subordinate garden areas and ancillary structures to their rear, resulting in an incongruous residential arrangement that fails to respond positively to its context. The development would therefore be contrary to Policies D12.2 and D12.3 of the Merton Local Plan (2024) and Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021).</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The proposed change of use of the existing ancillary building to an independent residential dwelling would result in an intensification of activity within the rear garden area, including increased pedestrian movements along the shared access and additional noise and disturbance associated with the occupation and use of the dwelling and its associated garden.&amp;nbsp; The proposal is in close proximity to neighbouring residential properties and their private amenity spaces and would result in unacceptable noise and disturbance to neighbouring occupiers. The development would therefore be contrary to &lt;span&gt;Policy D12.3(g) of the Merton Local Plan (2024)&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
